title: 'part stage' on a new untracked file, on a file changed only in the editor (not saved) and on line 39 of steps.rs while it has unsaved text: nothing wrong is staged, nothing is saved behind the user's back
folders: git-changes
expect-file: git-changes/src/util.rs :: ^pub fn double\(n: u32\) -> u32 \{\n    n \* 2\n
expect-file: git-changes/src/steps.rs :: ^fn step_1\(\) -> u32 \{\n    1\n
expect-file: git-changes/src/new_file.rs :: ^pub fn fresh\(\) \{\}\n$
forbid-log: script: ignoring

wait 3000
left changes
part stage src/new_file.rs 1
wait 1500
mark untracked
wait 600
edit src/util.rs 2 1
type // typed, not saved
key enter
wait 800
part stage src/util.rs 2
wait 1500
mark unsaved
wait 600
edit src/steps.rs 1 1
type // top
key enter
wait 800
part stage src/steps.rs 39
wait 1500
mark unsaved-shifted
wait 600
quit
wait 800
answer Close without saving
wait 1000
